# PBE on LiH with regularized orbitals, in the weak form of the semilocal xc
# potential.
#
# `xc_weak_gga true` never puts the semilocal xc potential -div(X), with
# X = 2 de/dsigma grad(rho), on the grid: X jumps at every nucleus, and
# differentiating that jump is noisy. Instead the divergence is moved onto the
# Green's function -- the orbital update gets the extra term 2 div(G Y_i) for a
# per-orbital vector field Y_i (the "flux"), and the xc block of the Fock matrix
# comes from XCOperator's matrix form rather than from xcnemo. See
# XCOperator::weak_xc_terms and Nemo::solve.
#
# The first deck to run the weak form at all, and it uses two orbitals on
# purpose: with one orbital (He) nothing is per-orbital, so the bookkeeping
# that pairs Y_i with orbital i -- through canonicalization and the BSH update
# -- is never exercised.
#
# CROSS-CHECK. The weak form is a rewriting, not a new approximation, so it
# must reproduce the ordinary multiplicative form. The same deck with
# `xc_weak_gga false` gives -8.0473162 at this single `protocol [1e-5]` rung
# (-8.0473189 here; both runs stop at an energy change of ~8e-6), and with the
# default protocol, ending at 1e-6, the two agree to 1.8 uHa (-8.0473240 vs
# -8.0473222, both stopping at an energy change of ~6e-7).
#
# NOT COVERED: canonicalization must rotate Y_i along with the orbitals. At
# convergence the canonicalizing transformation is essentially the identity,
# so dropping that rotation changes this deck's energy by only 3e-9 -- this
# deck would not catch it.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=nemo nemo_lih_pbe_weak.in)

dft
    xc          pbe
    protocol    [1e-5]
    localize    canon
    xc_weak_gga true
    maxiter     20
    econv       1e-5
    dconv       1e-3
end

nemo
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    Li  0.0  0.0  0.0
    H   0.0  0.0  3.0
end
